2
00:04:42,180 --> 00:04:44,820
[Based on Twentine's novel "The Story Untold" on jjwxc.net]

3
00:04:45,140 --> 00:04:48,020
[Episode 5]

4
00:04:51,630 --> 00:04:52,410
Make sure you count everything carefully.

5
00:04:52,620 --> 00:04:53,290
Don't worry, Ming.

6
00:04:54,300 --> 00:04:57,380
[Guan Gong, God of Wealth]

7
00:04:58,830 --> 00:04:59,410
Ming.

8
00:05:00,230 --> 00:05:00,730
Ming.

9
00:05:04,500 --> 00:05:11,260
[Guan Gong, God of Wealth]

10
00:05:11,560 --> 00:05:12,490
What's this supposed to mean, Ming?

11
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:14,620
Isn't Guan Gong's blade supposed to point upward?

12
00:05:14,910 --> 00:05:17,010
We're running a business, not fighting battles.

13
00:05:17,440 --> 00:05:18,890
The blade should point downward.

14
00:05:19,350 --> 00:05:22,370
Guan Gong should face the entrance

15
00:05:22,880 --> 00:05:24,450
to ward off evil spirits.

16
00:05:25,270 --> 00:05:26,420
With walls on both sides,

17
00:05:26,710 --> 00:05:28,660
the Azure Dragon on the left and White Tiger on the right.

18
00:05:35,540 --> 00:05:38,100
[Unknown Number]

19
00:05:39,620 --> 00:05:46,700
[Now. By the river.]

20
00:06:20,440 --> 00:06:21,210
Yan Zhengtao.

21
00:06:27,560 --> 00:06:28,980
Captain Yan.

22
00:06:30,470 --> 00:06:33,010
Mr. Bai sent me to invite you for tea.

23
00:06:35,390 --> 00:06:36,740
The car is waiting outside.

24
00:06:38,350 --> 00:06:39,130
Liu Wei.

25
00:06:42,470 --> 00:06:44,100
Isn't your boss impressive?

26
00:06:44,440 --> 00:06:45,860
He even knows Captain Yan.

27
00:07:06,760 --> 00:07:07,790
Tea from Yunshan.

28
00:07:09,150 --> 00:07:10,810
Prepared especially for you, Captain Yan.

29
00:07:12,830 --> 00:07:14,240
You've come a long way. It must've been tiring.

30
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:24,980
There's no need to rush.

31
00:07:26,790 --> 00:07:28,250
I prefer getting straight to the point.

32
00:07:29,710 --> 00:07:31,420
We've known each other for years.

33
00:07:32,270 --> 00:07:33,330
What do you want from me?

34
00:07:33,760 --> 00:07:34,330
Go ahead.

35
00:07:36,790 --> 00:07:37,500
That's true.

36
00:07:38,560 --> 00:07:39,660
We're old acquaintances.

37
00:07:41,030 --> 00:07:42,830
There's no point keeping secrets from you.

38
00:07:44,200 --> 00:07:47,620
In 2005, Mingkun was arrested within the border.

39
00:07:48,830 --> 00:07:52,500
In 2008, a logistics company was busted in Ruili.

40
00:07:53,320 --> 00:07:54,540
Three years ago,

41
00:07:55,470 --> 00:07:58,180
there was that 100-kilogram shipment of White Dragon Pearls in Simao.

42
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:01,570
All thanks to you, Captain Yan.

43
00:08:03,200 --> 00:08:04,860
You haven't arrested me all these years.

44
00:08:05,680 --> 00:08:07,010
Is that because you lack evidence,

45
00:08:07,880 --> 00:08:09,330
or because you've been going easy on me?

46
00:08:13,120 --> 00:08:14,620
It's not about going easy on anyone.

47
00:08:15,640 --> 00:08:17,420
We won't wrong an innocent person,

48
00:08:19,150 --> 00:08:20,890
and we'll never let a criminal go free.

49
00:08:23,230 --> 00:08:24,570
Not a single one will escape.

50
00:08:45,400 --> 00:08:47,140
I grew up in Kanan Village.

51
00:08:49,080 --> 00:08:49,900
In the village,

52
00:08:50,920 --> 00:08:52,570
a lot of people used drugs.

53
00:08:55,680 --> 00:08:57,140
My parents were no exception.

54
00:08:59,470 --> 00:09:01,060
Every day when I came home,

55
00:09:01,400 --> 00:09:04,140
I'd either find them fighting over their next fix,

56
00:09:04,710 --> 00:09:06,570
or they'd have taken too much

57
00:09:09,230 --> 00:09:10,180
and passed out.

58
00:09:10,680 --> 00:09:12,300
I was only about ten.

59
00:09:14,400 --> 00:09:15,450
I had a younger sister.

60
00:09:15,960 --> 00:09:16,730
She was eight.

61
00:09:18,230 --> 00:09:19,330
Every day, I'd take her

62
00:09:19,350 --> 00:09:20,610
out to beg for food.

63
00:09:24,400 --> 00:09:25,020
Brother.

64
00:09:26,350 --> 00:09:27,660
I'm so hungry.

65
00:09:27,680 --> 00:09:29,020
Most of the children in our village

66
00:09:29,990 --> 00:09:31,060
lived like that.

67
00:09:32,080 --> 00:09:33,300
Their families were addicted to drugs

68
00:09:35,040 --> 00:09:35,810
and desperately poor.

69
00:09:37,280 --> 00:09:39,210
Even getting enough to eat was a struggle.

70
00:09:56,160 --> 00:09:57,020
What are you doing?

71
00:09:58,110 --> 00:09:58,610
Brother!

72
00:09:59,510 --> 00:09:59,970
Brother!

73
00:10:00,400 --> 00:10:00,810
Let him go!

74
00:10:00,830 --> 00:10:03,020
Your parents still owe us money for drugs.

75
00:10:03,040 --> 00:10:04,300
And you have money to buy biscuits?

76
00:10:08,160 --> 00:10:09,490
Do you believe in fate?

77
00:10:11,230 --> 00:10:12,020
I don't.

78
00:10:16,110 --> 00:10:16,690
Brother!

79
00:10:16,960 --> 00:10:17,970
- Let her go! - Brother!

80
00:10:18,160 --> 00:10:18,970
Let him go!

81
00:10:18,990 --> 00:10:20,100
Let her go!

82
00:10:22,280 --> 00:10:23,180
But people

83
00:10:24,710 --> 00:10:27,210
usually don't become who they want to be.

84
00:10:27,560 --> 00:10:28,180
Bai Ji.

85
00:10:28,630 --> 00:10:31,140
You don't have to take drugs. You can sell them.

86
00:10:31,160 --> 00:10:32,330
It's your choice.

87
00:10:34,800 --> 00:10:35,900
Let me go!

88
00:10:36,680 --> 00:10:37,260
Brother!

89
00:10:38,230 --> 00:10:40,210
They become who they're forced to be.

90
00:10:43,350 --> 00:10:43,940
Fate,

91
00:10:44,960 --> 00:10:45,850
we can't choose.

92
00:10:49,080 --> 00:10:49,940
But our path,

93
00:10:51,440 --> 00:10:52,810
we can choose.

94
00:10:55,750 --> 00:10:57,420
So let me tell you a secret.

95
00:10:58,470 --> 00:11:01,450
I've never taken drugs.

96
00:11:02,440 --> 00:11:03,690
Not even once.

97
00:11:05,590 --> 00:11:07,330
I hate drugs, too.

98
00:11:08,990 --> 00:11:09,780
I really do.

99
00:11:11,510 --> 00:11:13,450
But if you have to blame someone,

100
00:11:14,350 --> 00:11:16,380
shouldn't you blame the people who take them?

101
00:11:16,830 --> 00:11:17,940
If they weren't so weak,

102
00:11:18,160 --> 00:11:20,210
if they weren't trying to escape reality,

103
00:11:20,230 --> 00:11:21,540
they wouldn't turn to drugs.

104
00:11:22,590 --> 00:11:24,850
So shouldn't you arrest the drug users first?

105
00:11:26,960 --> 00:11:27,690
Right?

106
00:11:30,870 --> 00:11:32,610
I'll arrest both users and dealers.

107
00:11:33,710 --> 00:11:36,060
Some users may have been driven to it by desperation.

108
00:11:36,830 --> 00:11:37,730
But dealers

109
00:11:39,110 --> 00:11:40,970
are utterly reprehensible.

110
00:11:42,680 --> 00:11:44,090
We certainly can't let them go.

111
00:11:59,680 --> 00:12:00,450
Sir.

112
00:12:16,630 --> 00:12:17,420
Sir.

113
00:12:22,470 --> 00:12:24,020
After all these years,

114
00:12:25,590 --> 00:12:27,090
it's time we settled things.

115
00:12:30,200 --> 00:12:32,020
But I truly believe

116
00:12:34,400 --> 00:12:36,090
we have a choice.

117
00:12:41,560 --> 00:12:43,490
Here, have something to eat first.

118
00:12:47,510 --> 00:12:48,490
I'll pour you some tea.

119
00:12:49,990 --> 00:12:50,970
Go ahead and eat.

120
00:12:52,110 --> 00:12:52,970
It's safe.

121
00:12:59,040 --> 00:13:00,420
If that's not enough,

122
00:13:01,280 --> 00:13:02,260
